var ROUTE=[["Narshe — prologue",1,"",["Terra starts at level 3 and should STAY there — no stat espers exist yet, so any level gained now is wasted. Her low level also drags the party average down, so every later recruit joins lower — including Banon, which is why the Lethe River fight is hard. That is a real cost, and worth it.","Fight the forced Magitek Armor battles through town to the Narshe Mines entrance (back row for everyone, no equipment changes possible yet).","Save at the first Save Point, then push north to Ymir.","Ymir fight: attack the HEAD only (1,600 HP) — never target the Shell (50,000 HP, cannot be killed, absorbs Lightning and heals from it, and counters any hit — including stray AoE — with ~65 dmg Megavolt on the whole party). Both Ymir entries register from a single win, so there's no need to (and no way to) kill the Shell.","After the scene, name Terra and Locke; grab the Elixir near the front door, then head out to a second mine entrance. The other mines chests UPGRADE — leave them for the World of Ruin.","In the narrow one-tile corridor before the Moogle room, open the menu and strip Terra's Mythril Knife and Buckler — hand them to Locke.","Take the tutorial if offered, then during the Moogle Defense open the menu between waves and STRIP MOG'S MYTHRIL SPEAR AND MYTHRIL SHIELD — once the sequence ends he is gone for good and takes them with him. That spear is Edgar's free weapon at Figaro Castle; miss it here and you'll have to buy one instead.","Fight through to the Guard Leader — this is where you learn the Guard Leader/Wind Slash Rage, the first of your nine combat-critical Rages. Locke can steal a Mythril Knife from him.","Visit the Adventuring School (beginner's classroom) chests, including the Silver Lobo Monster-in-a-Box fight.","Leave Narshe for the World Map."],[],[0,59,1],[0,1],"",null,null,null],["North Figaro — plains & desert",1,"",["Cross the grass/forest/desert terrain on the way to Figaro Castle.","Fight and steal from Leaf Bunny, Darkwind, Sand Ray and Alacran as encountered — these four also appear in the World of Balance Act 1 Cleanup section near the end of Act 1; checking one off there ticks it here too.","Try to meet at least one Alacran — its Stop-inflicting Rage becomes very useful soon.","Continue to the castle in the middle of the desert."],[],[22,23],[],"",null,null,null],["Figaro Castle",1,"",["Name Edgar, then explore the throne room area — skip the basement chests, they're World of Ruin only.","Loot the Tool Shop area chests (Potion, Antidote) and buy Bioblaster + Noiseblaster (Auto Crossbow is already given).","Loot the Item Shop's Gold Needle chest and the tower's Phoenix Down chest.","Speak to the High Priestess, then Edgar, then Kefka to advance.","Fight the forced Magitek Armor back-attack pincer.","Ride the Chocobo/castle to the southeastern desert cave to reach South Figaro Cave."],[],[],[2],"",[["Noiseblaster",500,"EDGAR — full price; no discount possible yet",null],["Bioblaster",750,"EDGAR — full price; needed later for the Imperial Elite",null],["Hold off on consumables",0,"what you have will reach South Figaro",null],["Give Edgar Mog's Mythril Spear",0,"free, unequipped back in the Narshe mines — no need to buy him a weapon",null]],null,null],["South Figaro Cave — first trek",1,"Entering Returner Hideout",["Turn encounters ON before entering — Foper, Hornet and Urok must each be fought at least once on THIS trek; boarding the raft afterward swaps the cave's encounter table and they're gone for good.","Fight through Foper/Hornet/Urok — Fire and Auto Crossbow work well.","Auto-heal at the Recovery Spring on the first screen.","At the first junction, skip the west Ether chest — it upgrades later, eventually reaching its final X-Potion form on the Locke and Celes trek.","At the next junction, skip the east Ether chest and the Phoenix Down chest near the stairs — both also upgrade later, into the World of Ruin.","Exit southeast to South Figaro town."],["g1"],[2],[3],"once",null,null,null],["South Figaro — town",1,"",["Explore the rich man's house — a Phoenix Down barrel outside, a hidden passage behind the upstairs bookcase leading to a Hyper Wrist + Hermes Sandals cell, and a clock room with 500/1000/1500 Gil chests.","Grab the free-standing items that never change (X-Potion between the shops, Green Cherry, Teleport Stone) and leave the ones that upgrade later (Eyedrops, Gold Needle, the two Potions). Other outdoor barrels/crates around town also upgrade, but three of them actually get WORSE — check the Chests list before assuming later is always better.","Shop: Great Sword for Terra, Plumed Hats/Heavy Shields/Cotton Robe/Kenpo Gi from the Armor Shop, Jeweled Ring + Star Pendants from the Relic Shop. Weapon upgrades are OPTIONAL for Edgar, Sabin, Shadow and Cyan — Tools, Blitz, Throw and Bushido all ignore weapon power — so spend the gil on Terra and Locke instead, who actually swing theirs.","Head to the South Figaro region: fight/steal from Belmodar (physical only — it COUNTERS any Magic command with Megavolt), Unseelie (steal the Buckler), and Mu. Steal a Mythril Claw from Belmodar (rare) — Sabin joins at Mt. Kolts and uses claws, so two is ideal. All three roam BOTH sides of Mt. Kolts, so you get a second chance outside the Returner Hideout if you miss them here — also summarized in the World of Balance Act 1 Cleanup section.","Rest for free at the house north of town — free beds and a Potion in the bucket there. That bucket (Sabin's house) is gone in the World of Ruin, so don't skip the Potion now.","Head northeast to the mountain trail and save before Mt. Kolts."],[],[24],[4,5,6],"",[["Great Sword",800,"TERRA — not Edgar, who already has Mog's free Mythril Spear",null],["Mythril Sword",450,"LOCKE",null],["Nothing for EDGAR",0,"he keeps Mog's Mythril Spear from the prologue — and Tools ignore weapon power entirely",null],["Heavy Shield",400,"EDGAR and LOCKE — buy two",null],["Plumed Hat",250,"EDGAR, TERRA, LOCKE, plus a spare for SABIN — buy four","Sabin"],["Cotton Robe",200,"TERRA",null],["Kenpo Gi",250,"LOCKE",null],["Buckler",200,"spare for SABIN, who joins at Mt. Kolts","Sabin"],["Sprint Shoes",1500,"optional quality-of-life only — Simmeh calls no relic here critical",null],["Potions ×25",1250,"party stock",null],["Phoenix Down ×5",2500,"party stock",null],["Antidote ×3",150,"more if you plan extra Mt. Kolts encounters",null],["Tent ×1–2",2400,"party stock",null],["DON'T buy status relics",0,"Hyper Wrist and Hermes Sandals are FREE in the rich man's basement, with 3,000 gil",null],["DON'T overstock",0,"Figaro Castle sells the same consumables at half price later with Edgar leading",null]],null,null],["Mt. Kolts",1,"",["Fight through Cirpius, Gorgias, Zaghrem, Trillium and Spritzer on the way up — this is where you learn the Trillium Rage, one of your nine combat-critical Rages. Zaghrem, Gorgias and Cirpius aren't required here, but keep an eye out for them while farming Trillium — also summarized in the World of Balance Act 1 Cleanup section near the end of Act 1.","Grab the two hidden-passage chests (southeast and northeast of the main cave — Main Gauche area and Gigas Glove) and the two Tent chests. Clear all four chests before you leave.","Before approaching Vargas: equip Edgar with the Gigas Glove (found here) and the Hyper Wrist (from South Figaro's rich man's house basement) — do this BEFORE the fight — then heal the party fully.","Quicksave on the field before triggering Vargas — you CANNOT save once the battle starts, and a Sabin death costs you the whole fight (both Ipoohs and the 720 damage), since you'd have to restart it from scratch.","Approach Vargas to start the fight.","VARGAS PHASE 1: he cannot be targeted until both Ipoohs die — not even by all-target attacks. The Ipoohs have 360 HP each and are weak to Fire — have Terra cast Fire on one at a time while Edgar uses Auto Crossbow/Bioblaster. Gale Cut hits the whole party for ~50, so keep everyone above that (Terra should focus on healing rather than damage).","Once 720 total damage has been dealt (you never actually need to deplete Vargas's HP), the scene triggers and Sabin takes over solo — Edgar's Bioblaster (140+ damage) is your best tool for reaching that total quickly, roughly five or six turns.","VARGAS PHASE 2 — PIXEL REMASTER TRAP: Raging Fist does NOTHING until Sabin's tutorial dialogue has fired. Act once with something else first (Aura Cannon or a plain attack) to trigger the tutorial, THEN input Raging Fist. Gale Cut no longer ignores Split Damage in PR — it does 100+ to a solo Sabin who has only about 132 HP, and he gets roughly two turns before a second Gale Cut kills him, so spend turn one triggering the tutorial and turn two on Raging Fist. Phase 2 ALSO opens with Doom Fist, which inflicts a separate ~60-second Doom countdown that is a straight Game Over on its own if it expires — don't dawdle even if Gale Cut looks survivable.","Vargas and both Ipoohs are separate bestiary entries. Locke can steal a rare Mythril Claw from Vargas.","MISSABLE SCENE: after beating Vargas, you can walk back to South Figaro and talk to Duncan's wife for a scene about Sabin — entering the Returner Hideout locks this out forever, so do it now if you want it.","Loot the Tent chest past Vargas, then continue to the Returner Hideout."],[],[25,60],[7],"wob",null,null,null],["Returner Hideout",1,"Leaving the hideout",["General rule for all three upcoming scenario splits: strip a departing character at the LAST point you still control their movement, NOT when the scenario \"ends\" — cutscenes lock the menu before you get the chance.","Explore the storeroom area for the Air Knife/Phoenix Down/Knight's Code chests, an Antidote/Ether, and a hidden-passage White Cape (nine containers here total, none available in the World of Ruin). The walk here from Mt. Kolts has no new enemies — same Belmodar, Unseelie and Mu as before, so this is your last chance at them if you skipped them near South Figaro.","Visit the meeting room east of the entrance: talk to Sabin, grab the Green Cherry pot, and note this is the first shop selling Hi-Potions — stock up here.","Return to Edgar's room and open the Hi-Potion chest.","Talk to everyone, then speak to Banon just outside the exit.","Before accepting his request, strip Locke of ALL his gear (it returns to the shared pool) — this is the actual swap point, not the raft itself. He leaves for his own scenario the instant you accept and takes everything he's still wearing with him, and the raft party (fighting Ultros next) needs that gear.","Choose between the Gauntlet and the Genji Glove — you can only ever get one this way. Say YES to Banon for the Gauntlet; yes on the first, second, or third ask all work, so saying no the first time costs nothing. To get the Genji Glove instead, say no, then talk to the Returner in the storeroom — he hands it over, but that makes Banon withhold the Gauntlet permanently. Saying no three times without talking to the Returner only changes the cutscene (Terra's introspection replaces the strategy meeting) and still lets you say yes later. You'll get a Genji Glove from a chest in the Cave to the Sealed Gate anyway, and it's also farmable later via Metamorphose; the Gauntlet only appears at two other points, both much later, so it's genuinely quantity-limited — take it here. CORRECTED PR NOTE: the Genji Glove is still the stronger relic overall — Pixel Remaster only fixed a bug where its dual-wield penalty was wrongly hitting single-weapon use (which nerfed, not buffed, its old numbers); the Gauntlet was never touched. So taking the Gauntlet here is a scarcity call, not a power call.","Accept Banon's request to trigger the scene where he replaces Locke in the party.","Head south and board the raft."],["g2"],[],[8],"wob",[["Hi-Potion",0,"FIRST place in the game that sells them — stock up hard",null],["Phoenix Down / Antidote / Tent",0,"item shop only; there are no relics or equipment here",null],["FREE INN",0,"the inn here costs nothing. Rest to full before boarding the raft — Banon starts the Ultros fight at whatever HP he has now",null]],null,null],["Lethe River",1,"",["At the first intersection, go left; use the Save Point cave. Lesser Lopros, Nautiloid and Exocite may turn up along the way — not required here, also summarized in the World of Balance Act 1 Cleanup section near the end of Act 1.","At the next intersection, go left again (or grind on the loop if desired); use the second Save Point.","ULTROS #1 — Banon must survive this fight; if he is KO'd it is an instant Game Over, not a normal loss. Put EVERYONE in the back row, Banon included — Tentacle is a physical attack, so the row halves it. Track Ultros' 3-turn attack script and be ready to have Banon Defend at full HP right before his Banon-targeting Tentacle hit. Banon's Pray command (renamed from \"Health\" pre-PR) heals the whole party — he should be casting it most turns rather than attacking. Heal Terra when Ultros' scripted 10-second attack targets her, then have her nuke with Fire.","If Banon feels too fragile for this or the scenario ahead, you can safely power-level HIM alone: set EXP to 4x, KO Terra, Edgar and Sabin, and let Banon finish fights solo — KO'd characters gain no EXP, so only he levels. This is safe ONLY because Banon leaves at the end of his own scenario, before Celes, Cyan and Gau join — do the Terra/Edgar/Banon scenario FIRST so his level never enters their averaging. Set EXP back to 0x the moment he is comfortable.","After the win, watch the scenes — Sabin is swept away, which triggers the party splitting into three separate scenarios here.","Do the scenarios in order: Terra/Edgar/Banon first (easiest, and lets you strip gear risk-free), then Locke, then Sabin last (longest and hardest, so it should inherit everything)."],[],[26,61],[],"wob",null,null,null],["Terra / Edgar / Banon scenario — Narshe",1,"",["Do this scenario first among the three splits — it is the easiest, and it lets you strip gear for the other two risk-free.","Cross the North Figaro region back to Narshe — the river drops you east of Narshe and the guards block the front gate, so you'll need to go back in through the mines. Valeor and Wild Rat only appear in the west mines corridor you use here, though the corridor itself is walkable again for the rest of the World of Balance — also summarized in the World of Balance Act 1 Cleanup section.","Enter through the secret passage west of the Adventuring School.","Fight through the Wererat/Bandit cave, then the Valeor/Wild Rat mine.","SECURITY CHECKPOINT: on entering, a light TRACES the correct route across the room — watch it, then walk the same path. There is no fixed map to memorize; the game shows you every time. IF YOU STRAY: eight lights surround you — SEVEN BLUE, ONE ORANGE/GOLD. Face the GOLD one and interact; they scatter and nothing happens. Miss the gold one and you fight two undead, then get sent back to the room's start — no progress lost, just time. CORRECTED: the strays themselves have no bestiary entries, but Darkside, Specter and Eukaryote ARE valid Rages obtainable ONLY here — stray on purpose at least once if you're going for a full Rage list, at no bestiary cost either way. There are no other random encounters in this room at all, and in the World of Ruin the checkpoint stops triggering entirely.","Past the checkpoint the Moogle room opens — skip the Rune Blade chest, it upgrades to a Ribbon later — and continue past the other chests and the Save Point. There's a healing pot next to Banon here, a Pixel Remaster addition.","Before talking to Arvis, strip Terra and Edgar COMPLETELY — relics included — along with any Bandanas needed later. Talking to Arvis ends the scenario immediately with no menu access after, and anything still worn by Terra or Edgar is locked to them, unavailable to Locke and Sabin.","Talk to Arvis to end the scenario."],[],[5],[9],"once",null,null,null],["Locke's scenario — South Figaro",1,"Scenario end",["Equip Locke from the shared pool first — he is solo and fragile. Give him the Main Gauche, Mythril Shield, Bandana, Kenpo Gi, plus White Cape and Hermes Sandals if they're free, then move him to the Front Row.","Work through the disguise puzzle (steal a Merchant outfit, get the Cider from the Pub basement Merchant, learn the password \"Courage\") to reach the Old Man's basement passage — do NOT use the Kutan/Moghan glitch to skip it. Note: there's a HEAVY ARMOR blocking a passage in town — solo Locke will almost certainly lose that fight, so skip it here; that entry is also available later at the Battle of Narshe.","Recruit Celes in the secret passage, gear her up, and grab the Old Clock Key from the sleeping guard.","Loot the storage-room chests (Iron Armor, Heavy Shield, Great Sword, Hi-Ether, X-Potion, Ribbon, Earring) and unlock the clock door.","Exit to the World Map, then re-enter South Figaro Cave for the second trek — the cave swaps its encounter table between treks, so this pass brings new enemies: Acrophies, Cartagra and Gold Bear, which appear only on this second trek.","LEAVE the Thunder Rod chest — it becomes a HERO'S RING in the World of Ruin. Breaking the rod would one-shot Tunnel Armor, but the ring is the better prize and you're guaranteed a return trip. TAKE the X-Potion at the west end of the main cave instead — it is already at its final value and never upgrades again.","Before the boss, strip Locke and Celes COMPLETELY of any transferable gear needed for Sabin's scenario — this is your LAST menu access; you cannot change equipment during the fight, and the scenario ends immediately after it.","Fight Tunnel Armor (without the rod): have Celes use RUNIC every single available turn to eat its magic, Locke attacks, and use Potions to heal — long but not dangerous. Re-select Runic only AFTER it absorbs something — choosing any other command for Celes drops the stance. Hermes Sandals on Celes give her auto-Haste so she can keep Runic up between its casts."],[],[3,4],[16,17],"once",null,null,null],["Sabin's scenario — overworld to the Imperial Camp",1,"",["Recruit Shadow from the traveling merchant outside the starting house (buy Shurikens for Throw).","Cross the grass/forest terrain toward the desert, fighting Stray Cat, Aepyornis, Nettlehopper and Chippirabbit as encountered — this walk is where that encounter group actually lives, not inside the camp itself. GRASS tends to favor Aepyornis and Chippirabbit while FOREST tends to favor Nettlehopper and Stray Cat, but this is only a tendency, not a hard split — player reports (and PR guides that hedge with \"usually\") confirm Stray Cat can show up on grass too, and the underlying odds come from an older console datamine that Pixel Remaster may have shuffled, so treat tile type as a lean, not a rule.","Prioritize meeting at least one STRAY CAT here — it is missable and gives Gau's strongest physical Rage (Cat Scratch, x4 damage), confirmed as the strongest single-target Rage available for a long while. Every formation you fight elsewhere first only dilutes the Veldt pool, so it's worth prioritizing now. If Chippirabbit specifically is still missing, grass remains the better bet, just not a guarantee.","Aepyornis, Nettlehopper and Chippirabbit are NOT time-critical — this terrain stays walkable, and flyable once you have the airship, for the rest of the World of Balance, so those three are also summarized in the World of Balance Act 1 Cleanup section near the end of Act 1.","All four of these enemies are World of Balance only — the World of Ruin version of this ground swaps in Tumbleweed, Crawler, Sprinter and Lycaon instead.","Save before entering the \"desert,\" which is actually the Imperial Camp."],[],[6,63],[],"wob",null,null,null],["Sabin's scenario — Imperial Camp",1,"Leaving the camp",["Equip Sabin from the shared pool (Locke/Celes gear is now available if you did the scenarios in the recommended order) — anything still worn by Locke or Celes is unavailable to him.","Name and take control of Cyan; fight the Leader for a Black Belt (reset if it drops a Phoenix Down instead).","Kick (not hit) the tent chest to force the mandatory Doberman fight — this is the only place to ever meet it, and its Veldt appearance is mandatory.","Grab the Barrier Ring by jumping down behind the west tent.","Open the Mythril Glove chest, then the Satellite box, fighting Satellite for the Star Pendant/Green Beret — missable here, but it's repeatable on the Veldt afterward, so farm the other three Green Berets there later.","Provoke Kefka three times (he flees each time) while clearing the surrounding Imperial Soldiers/Templars.","Leave the camp for good."],["g4"],[7],[10],"once",null,null,["OPTIONAL: Shadow offers to join Sabin here for free — worth taking. He leaves automatically at Baren Falls either way, so there's no downside to accepting"]],["Sabin's scenario — Doma Castle",1,"",["Cyan joins here, across two segments — first a siege you control him through, second inside the castle after the water is poisoned.","Control switches to Cyan outside the gates for the siege segment — the objective is the Captain (bestiary #36), not the rank-and-file soldiers.","The wall-climbing troopers all start the same 2x Imperial Soldier fight — one is enough for the bestiary/Rage entry (optional; every soldier group is identical, the rest give nothing), then beat the Captain to end the siege.","Menu is open on Cyan here — equip him from the shared pool before he departs with Sabin/Shadow; he keeps whatever you give him when he joins.","Control returns to Sabin/Shadow in the Imperial Camp; explore, then Kefka poisons Doma's water and flees to the castle.","Control switches back to Cyan inside the castle — go down to the throne room and watch the king die.","The Remedy Pot is the only obtainable item left in the whole castle now — every other treasure is blocked off.","Go through either of the two bottom doors past the throne room (both lead to the same waiting-area room, via the carpeted stairs south of the throne room then the south-east room) and take the Remedy from the pot on the right.","Other nearby doors are safe to check too — e.g. a top-right door that's just a dead end (Cyan steps back out saying \"Here too...\").","DO NOT enter the upper-right family-scene door yet if you still want the Remedy first — it triggers the family scene and ends the segment on the spot.","Enter the upper-right door when ready: Cyan finds his wife and son, swears revenge, and the segment ends, sending him to the Imperial Camp to join the party.","Not a hard loss if you trigger it early — Cyan's Dream later carries the same treasures, obtainable in one location or the other."],[],[],[11],"wob",null,null,null],["Sabin's scenario — Phantom Forest",1,"",["Enter the forest southeast of Doma Castle with Sabin (Cyan and, if he's stuck around, Shadow).","Fight through Ghost/Poplium encounters — Ghost's Rage is combat-critical and this is the only source for it in this scenario; Poplium isn't required here (it's also summarized in the World of Balance — Act 1 Cleanup section near the end of Act 1).","Always take the exit at the top of the screen; other exits loop you back.","Step on the Recovery Spring tile to auto-heal before continuing.","Reach the wrecked train at the far side of the forest and board it to start the Phantom Train segment."],[],[8,65],[],"wob",null,null,null],["Sabin's scenario — Phantom Train",1,"Leaving the train",["Board the train; Shadow can be revived/used again safely now that he's trapped aboard (he won't flee mid-train).","Work through the cars, picking up the Tent, Earring, second Tent, Phoenix Down x2, and Sniper Eye chests along the way — seven chest entries total here, not the two-chest \"Simmeh route\" shortcut.","Optionally accept a temporary Ghost ally at one of the early cars (he leaves automatically before the locomotive).","Open the chest in the fourth suite when Siegfried appears — he steals its contents regardless of the fight's outcome, and it can never be recovered.","Defeat the Apparition monster-in-a-box for a Hyper Wrist.","Reach the locomotive, flip the correct pressure valves, then fight the Phantom Train boss — Oversoul's Rage is combat-critical and this is the only place it's learnable.","Watch the Cyan family cutscene and exit to the overworld."],["g5"],[9],[12],"once",null,null,null],["Sabin's scenario — Baren Falls",1,"",["Immediately after leaving the Phantom Train you land on a field screen with full menu access — this, not the train itself, is your true last chance to STRIP SHADOW'S EQUIPMENT before he leaves the party.","Walk east into the cave and head toward the falls.","Dive down the falls: fight waves of Opinicus Fish for about 60 seconds.","Rhizopas boss appears after the wave timer — burst it down with strong single-target hits (Fang, Aura Cannon) before it gets off El Nino.","Shadow automatically leaves the party the moment you reach the falls, taking whatever he's still wearing — he isn't recruitable again until the Kohlingen tavern.","You land on the Veldt and meet Gau, who runs off — proceed to the next stop."],[],[10],[],"once",null,null,null],["Sabin's scenario — Mobliz",1,"",["Enter Mobliz.","Buy at least one Dried Meat from the item shop — the only source in the game, and required to recruit Gau.","Grab the Elixir from the clock in the mailman's house — this one is still here in the World of Ruin too.","Head back out to the Veldt."],[],[],[13],"",[["Mythril Claw",800,"SABIN",null],["Kotetsu",800,"CYAN",null],["Magus Hat",600,"buy now for much later — Terra/Strago","Strago"],["White Cape ×2 extra",10000,"you want three in total",null],["Dried Meat",150,"required to recruit GAU on the Veldt","Gau"],["Green Berets are FREE",0,"Satellites in Veldt group 8 always drop one — farm two",null]],null,null],["Sabin's scenario — The Veldt (recruiting Gau)",1,"",["You land here straight after Baren Falls and Gau runs off — you can't recruit him yet without Dried Meat.","Return to the Veldt with Dried Meat bought in Mobliz, then fight formations until Gau appears saying he's hungry.","Use the Dried Meat item on him instead of attacking — he joins after the ensuing dialogue.","Gau's join level is your PARTY AVERAGE plus a fixed +2 bonus — the +2 is fixed, the resulting number isn't. It lands around 7 on this route's usual pace, but moves if your average does, and it's been dragging every later join (Shadow included) up ever since.","Before leaving, farm Rages from other formations and farm Green Berets from Satellite drops (four total is the target) — this is the only Veldt access for a long stretch.","Continue on to the Serpent Trench."],[],[],[],"",null,null,null],["Sabin's scenario — Serpent Trench",1,"",["Board the raft; it's a mostly-automatic ride with two branch-point choices.","Pick the right fork at both decision points to reach the two side caves — these chests aren't available in the World of Ruin, so take both now.","First cave: grab the X-Potion chest.","Second cave: climb the stairs, hit the switch to drain the flooded section, drop through the hole, and grab the Green Beret chest.","Fight Anguiform (Rage wanted later for Cranes), Aspiran (Rage wanted for Ultros at the Opera House), and Actinian formations along the way to seed their Veldt pools.","Fighting them here only unlocks the Veldt formation — Gau still has to fight that same formation once ON THE VELDT to actually learn the Rage. Make a Veldt stop before the Opera House or Aspiran won't be usable yet. (Actinian isn't required here — it's also summarized in the World of Balance — Act 1 Cleanup section, as long as you fly the raft entrance again before triggering the Floating Continent.)","Ride out to Nikeah to end the trench segment."],[],[11,64],[14],"wob",null,null,null],["Sabin's scenario — Nikeah",1,"Boarding the ship",["Enter Nikeah — this is the last stop of Sabin's scenario.","Grab the Elixir from the clock in the Inn.","Shop for any last gear/items before boarding — this is your last chance to spend before the Narshe battle.","Head to the docks and board the ship to end Sabin's scenario; everyone meets up at Narshe."],[],[],[15],"",[["Silk Robe",600,"CELES — the only notable item in Nikeah",null],["Mythril Spear",800,"MOG uses spears and joins much later","Mog"]],null,null],["Battle of Narshe",1,"Defeating Kefka",["At the save point, assign all 7 available characters (Terra, Locke, Edgar, Sabin, Celes, Cyan, Gau) across three teams — everyone fights here, nobody sits this one out.","Equip everyone before setting off — save the Green Berets for Celes/Terra last.","Build the main combat team around Celes + Gau, adding Edgar and Sabin (Terra or Sabin can fill the fourth slot); it does 100% of the heavy lifting so give it the best gear — strip Locke's gear onto it if needed.","Send the other two teams to intercept the soldier waves blocking their own path to Banon — they fight too, just weaker squads rather than a boss, so give them the leftover gear. Locke solo is popular here for repeatable Steals against the runner enemy.","Cut through the enemies rather than dodging them — fight through both the green squads (Corporal/Hunting Hound) and the brown squads (Fidor/Heavy Armor); you need at least one of each for bestiary/Rage entries.","HEAVY ARMOR (bestiary #24) comes from the brown squads here — this is the safer place to take that entry rather than soloing it in South Figaro. It's the rarer of the two brown formations, so don't rush to Kefka before you've seen one.","Against Heavy Armor, avoid spell-casting Rages while Celes is in the party — she triggers its Magitek Barrier, granting it Protect and Reflect. Use defense-ignoring physicals instead (Raging Fist, Fang). Without Celes present, it's just weak to Lightning and Water.","Defeat the Hell's Rider commander blocking the final approach.","Speak to Kefka to trigger the boss fight and defeat or flee him to end the battle.","The treasure house chests in Narshe open up after this battle — worth a stop before moving on."],["g6"],[12],[18],"once",[["Weapon and armour upgrades",0,"first time Narshe's shops are usable — big jump over scenario gear",null],["Barrier Ring",500,"Shell when critically wounded, plus Magic +2",null],["Mythril Shield",1200,"front-line upgrade",null],["Silk Robe",600,"CELES",null],["Don't buy an Earring or Thief's Bracer yet",0,"both are free from the same Narshe treasure-house chest, but it's still locked — it doesn't open until AFTER the Magitek Factory. Buy here only if you need one before then",null],["Hold consumables",0,"Figaro Castle is half price with Edgar leading",null]],null,["MUST: Celes + Gau on the main team","RECOMMENDED: add Edgar + Sabin to round it out","Locke CAN fight if you keep him — he's just the weakest link, so his gear is better spent on the four above"]],["Kohlingen & region",1,"",["Explore Kohlingen: grab the Green Beret chest and the Elixir from the clock in Rachel's house.","Visit the House at Dragon's Neck for the Hero's Ring in the pot (World of Balance only — the house is gone in the World of Ruin).","Shadow is optional from here on — grab him whenever you run into him rather than saving it for a specific stop. He's guaranteed for 3,000 gil at the Kohlingen tavern, the only free-roam recruit point in the World of Balance (the South Figaro bar sighting is name-only, not a recruit point — you can't actually hire him there).","Once he's in the party: sleeping at inns has a 50% chance each time to trigger one of his 4 backstory dreams (a 5th plays automatically later in the story) — keep resting at the same inn to cycle through them. Doesn't work at free/scripted beds like Figaro Castle or Thamasa.","Sweep the plains/forest quintet (Vulture, Iron Fist, Bloodfang, Rock Wasp, Paraladia) and Fossil Dragon now, or defer to the World of Balance — Act 1 Cleanup section near the end of Act 1."],[],[27,28],[19,20],"",null,null,null],["Jidoor",1,"",["Walk through Jidoor.","The Auction House is here but locked until you have the Blackjack (after the Magitek Factory) — nothing to buy yet; it's tracked at the \"Narshe, the return\" stop.","Continue on toward Zozo."],[],[],[21],"",[["Earring",5000,"magic boost, stacks if two characters wear one",null],["Sniper Eye",3000,"physicals never miss",null],["Peace Ring",3000,"blocks berserk + confusion",null],["Ninja Gear",1100,"Shadow","Shadow"],["White Dress",2200,"women's armour — also fits Terra and Celes","Relm"]],null,null],["Zozo",1,"",["No shops in Zozo — arrive stocked.","Enter Zozo and talk to townsfolk for clock-time clues — everyone lies except the man just outside the Inn.","Solve the clock puzzle (answer: 6:10:50) on the ground floor of the Inn-marked building (the one with the bed icon) to reveal the secret staircase — reward is the Chainsaw, an Edgar Tool.","Sweep the town for its nine treasure chests — several are easy to walk past.","Rage-farm Gobbledygook here (fight it with Gau active) — it's combat-critical later at the Cave to the Sealed Gate (Vanish for Number 024), so confirm it's actually banked before that stop, not just encountered. Harvester, Hill Gigas, and Veil Dancer aren't required here but may turn up while farming — also summarized in the World of Balance — Act 1 Cleanup section near the end of Act 1.","Fight toward Dadaluma; he counters Fight, Magic, and Steal, so lean on Tools/Blitz/Bushido/Rage instead. He's poison-weak, so Trillium Rage (Poison Touch, from Mt. Kolts) helps — confirm it's been re-fought with Gau present since Mt. Kolts, or it isn't banked yet.","Defeat Dadaluma to open the top of the tower.","Collect Ramuh, Kirin, Siren, and Cait Sith automatically at the top — free and automatic, nothing to buy or unlock, not related to the Auction House at all.","Continue the story with Terra.","Whichever pub you picked Shadow up from (Kohlingen's tavern is the guaranteed one — see that stop), he joins at your CURRENT PARTY AVERAGE, not a fixed level. That average isn't just earned EXP: Gau's join back on the Veldt was party-average+2, a fixed bonus rather than a fixed number, and it's been nudging the average up ever since — so even at a strict 0x run, don't be surprised if Shadow already matches everyone else.","Shadow leaves with whatever he is wearing — STRIP HIM before dropping him in Narshe. Same every time he departs; he's transient throughout the World of Balance."],[],[29,62],[22],"",null,null,null],["Opera House",1,"Stopping the weight",["Perform the opera as Celes (fixed correct lines: 'Oh my hero...', 'I'm the darkness', 'Must my...').","Fight the rafter rats — Stunner (fire-weak) and Goetia (ice-weak).","Continue through the following sequence and defeat Ultros — Aspiran Rage (Gigavolt) helps here, so confirm it's actually banked from a Veldt trip since Serpent Trench, not just fought there.","Setzer joins peacefully right after — no fight is needed to recruit him, he's fooled by Celes' coin trick.","Take the Blackjack to leave."],["g7"],[13],[],"once",null,null,null],["Southern Continent & Veldt forest",1,"",["Explore the Southern Continent for story progression and any available chests.","Detour to the Veldt to encounter/farm the enemies listed for bestiary completion — Litwor Chicken, Joker, Don, Wyvern, Grasswyrm, Bug, and Grenade — also summarized in the World of Balance — Act 1 Cleanup section near the end of Act 1.","Intangir is deferred to Triangle Island once the airship is available — it stays put there and is Gau's strongest Rage."],[],[30,31],[],"",null,null,null],["Albrook & Maranda",1,"",["Visit Albrook and open both chests in the Armor Shop — they're empty but still count toward the treasure checklist.","Visit Maranda for its story beat and any chests.","Continue on toward the Magitek Factory."],[],[],[23,24],"",[["Reflect Ring ×3",18000,"TOP PRIORITY — Albrook. You need four total; one is found in Narshe",null],["Priest's Miter ×4",12000,"magic evasion for the Ifrit/Shiva fight",null],["Hermes Sandals",7000,"Tzen — bring your total to four",null],["Mythril Mail",3500,"LOCKE, CELES and your fourth",null],["White Dress",2200,"RELM joins in Thamasa","Relm"],["Ninja Gear",1100,"SHADOW, and GAU wears it too","Shadow"],["Teleport Stone",700,"buy a stack",null]],null,null],["Magitek Factory (IMRF)",1,"Meeting Setzer to leave",["No shops inside the factory and no way back once you enter — restock Hi-Potions and Phoenix Downs before entering.","There's no Soul Shrine in Pixel Remaster, so there's no second chance at it — a PR-specific trap to keep in mind here.","Lead with your third character so the red Magna Roader spawns — it will not spawn behind Locke, Edgar, or Gau.","Explore the Research Facility: grab Ifrit (it also gates Drain for everyone but Terra) and find the hidden Stoneblade passage.","Quicksave before the rail-cart escape sequence.","Ride the cart escape, fighting off pursuers.","Defeat Number 128 at the end of the escape — a center body plus Left and Right Blade. Ghost Rage (Thundara) helps here.","Steal Kazekiri #1 from Number 128 — this is a base-rate steal, not a boosted one, since the Thief's Bracer doesn't exist yet at this point in the route (its only sources are a Narshe chest that opens AFTER this trip, and a Tzen shop in the World of Ruin). Not technically missable, but it stays this rare for a long time afterward, so it's worth resetting for if you whiff it.","Meet Setzer to leave — escaping Vector afterward throws two Cranes at you (both weak to Water); Anguiform Rage's Aqua Breath (from Serpent Trench) hits both at once, so confirm it's banked."],["g8","g9"],[14],[25,26],"once",null,null,["Lead with anyone EXCEPT Locke, Edgar or Gau — the red Magna Roader (X-Ether steal) won't spawn behind them"]],["Narshe — the return",1,"",["Open the previously locked treasure-house chest in Narshe, now available.","Detour to the Jidoor Auction House and bid on Golem (~20,000 gil) and Zona Seeker (~10,000 gil) — your first +2 espers.","Handle any remaining Narshe story/shopping business.","If passing through Figaro Castle with both Edgar and Sabin present, sleep in the beds — it triggers a bonus scene that isn't possible on the first visit."],[],[],[27],"",[["Figaro Castle: Drill",3000,"EDGAR — lead with him for 50% off; Flash is optional, no fight needs it",null],["Jidoor Auction House: Golem + Zona Seeker",30000,"your first +2 espers — top priority",null],["Jidoor Auction House: Seraph",3000,"optional — teaches nothing new but faster",null],["Hero's Ring is FREE",0,"Dragon's Neck cabin pot — give it to Gau",null],["Tiara",3000,"RELM joins in Thamasa","Relm"],["Poison Rod",1500,"STRAGO joins in Thamasa — first rod sold anywhere","Strago"]],null,null],["Lone Wolf",1,"Choice made",["Travel to the Narshe cliffs area to trigger the Lone Wolf/Mog scene.","Wait a moment — Mog knocks Lone Wolf back.","Choose to save MOG, not Lone Wolf's offered Gold Hairpin — this recruits Mog; picking the Hairpin instead loses one of his Dances."],["g10"],[],[],"once",null,null,null],["Cave to the Sealed Gate",1,"Boarding the ship at Albrook",["Do NOT use any 'no encounters' effect here — the biggest trap in this area is walking through with encounters off. Five bestiary entries lock here, along with the Ultima Weapon, Heiji's Jitte, and Kazekiri #2, so don't skip encounters or leave without them — story-critical fights and treasures require normal encounters.","Number 024 is here — Gobbledygook Rage (Vanish) is combat-critical for it, so confirm it's actually banked from Zozo before this fight, not just encountered there.","Work through the cave, collecting its eighteen chests, including four hidden floor items.","Grab the Assassin's Dagger, Elixir, Magicite Shards, Hi-Ether, and the Ultima Weapon in the multi-chest room.","Get Heiji's Jitte from the upper-right ledge chest in the first small lava room.","Cross the new bridge for the Genji Glove.","Get Kazekiri #2.","Reach and pass through the Sealed Gate to conclude the stop."],["g11"],[15],[28],"wob",null,null,null],["Vector & Imperial Palace",1,"Banquet end",["Save before entering — this is a one-shot sequence, and you need roughly 90 of the 93 maximum points for all five reward thresholds, so treat it as a full-marks run rather than a best-effort one (44 points come from the four-minute soldier walkabout, 49 from the banquet itself).","During the 4-minute soldier walkabout, talk to all 24 soldiers — 1 point each. The two Elite Soldiers in Gestahl's throne room do NOT count, and neither does Kefka in his cell — skip Kefka, he burns a large slice of the timer.","Let the four hostile soldiers (three normal, one armored) fight you and win them — worth 6 points each (1 for talking + 5 for the win), versus only 1 point if you lose or flee.","Skip treasure chests during the timer — the palace chests stay open afterward, so there's no rush.","Once you have all 24 soldiers, you can end the timer early through a top door in the throne room.","At the banquet, answer 'To our homelands' (5), 'Leave him in jail' (5), and 'That was inexcusable' (5).","Ask Gestahl all three optional questions, once each (2 points apiece) — asking one twice is MINUS 10. He then asks which you asked first; answering correctly is worth 5, so remember the order.","During Cid's break, fight the Imperial Elite (poison-weak, via a non-Gestahl NPC after 'Take a break') within the 2-minute limit for 5 points — failing scores 0. Trillium Rage, Bioblaster, and Bio help here — same Trillium banking check as Zozo applies.","Answer 'That your war is truly over,' then say Yes the first time you're asked to board the ship — saying no first forfeits the bonus even if you say yes afterward.","On the remaining prompts, pick the conciliatory option each time (e.g. trusting Terra whether she spied or not).","Collect rewards on the way out based on cumulative point thresholds: South Figaro is liberated regardless of score / 50+ reopens Doma Castle / 67+ unlocks the Observation Post armory (12 chests) / 77+ grants the Tintinnabulum / 90+ grants the Ward Bangle. The Tintinnabulum and Ward Bangle are GIFT rewards here, not chests — they appear nowhere else on this route."],["g12"],[16],[29,30],"once",null,null,null],["Albrook — second visit",1,"",["Restock supplies — last chance before sailing to Thamasa.","Grab the Teleport Stone from the crate near the docks entrance.","Board the ship to Thamasa."],[],[],[31],"",null,null,null],["Thamasa & Crescent Island",1,"Before the Esper Caves",["Explore Thamasa town and loot its five barrels — they're all gone after the Esper Caves.","Get the Memento Ring hidden upstairs in Strago's house (examine the wall by the table).","Strago and Relm join automatically.","Proceed through the story with General Leo as a temporary guest — he does not survive, so do not hand him anything you want back.","Strago learns a Lore by seeing it used and WINNING the fight (fleeing cancels it) — his Lores bypass Reflect and Runic, which pairs well with Celes. Gau's Rages and Relm's Sketch/Control can teach him Lores too, not just enemies. Briareus, Devourer, and Chimera are also summarized in the World of Balance — Act 1 Cleanup section near the end of Act 1.","Continue on to the Esper Caves."],[],[32],[32],"timed",[["Shops stay shut",0,"Thamasa will not sell until the Cave to the Sealed Gate is done",null],["Ice Rod ×1 minimum",3000,"absolute minimum — required for Flame Eater",null],["Thunder Rod ×3",9000,"for the fast Ultros strategy in the Esper Cave",null],["Ice Rod ×7–8 + Flame Rod ×3–4",30000,"for a fast Typhon + Ultros on the FC approach",null],["Buy a dozen of each if flush",0,"that will last the rest of the game",null],["Mythril Rod",500,"STRAGO joins here",null],["Gaia Gear",6000,"TERRA, LOCKE, STRAGO",null]],null,null],["Burning House",1,"Engaging Flame Eater",["Enter as Terra/Locke/Strago; equip Strago with an esper/relics before going in — he already knows three Lores from the start: Aqua Breath, Revenge Blast, and Stone","Fight through the Balloon formations in rooms 2-5 (they come in packs of ~3, sometimes 6) — Aqua Breath hits all enemies with water and sweeps these fire-based Balloons","Optionally stand still against a lone Balloon and let it Self-Destruct to teach Strago the Lore","Grab the Flame Rod (room 4, right-hand door) and Ice Rod (room 5, right-hand door) chests","Equip Shiva if available before the top floor, then engage Flame Eater","Flame Eater is fire too — use Aqua Breath, Blizzara, or break an Ice Rod for a fast kill (it's weak to Ice)","Survive the Balloon/Grenade reinforcements it summons and finish it off"],["g13"],[17],[33],"once",null,null,null],["Triangle Island",1,"",["Sail to Triangle Island and find the small forest near one tip where Intangir hides","Save before engaging; do NOT fight it while badly underleveled — at level 6 its Meteor counter hits each character for 850-968, a one-shot kill for a low-level party","Come back once Gau is level 26 from the Esper Cave grind, before leaving for the Floating Continent — that is the window","It starts Invisible, and only a spell can touch it. Cast Stop on it first — Stop is a status weakness that deals no damage, so it doesn't trigger the Meteor counter — to break Invisibility and freeze it (if it wakes with 1,280 HP or less it flees instead of fighting, with no bestiary entry, so keep Stop cycling)","Cycle Stop on it every couple of rounds, re-casting before it wears off (Hermes Sandals for auto-Haste help you outpace the timer), and hit it with non-elemental damage while it's frozen — it absorbs every element. Gau's Stray Cat rage (Cat Scratch, x4) is ideal; Strago's Stone Lore, which he knows from the moment he joins, does 8x damage to same-level enemies and at 26 shreds Intangir; Edgar's Drill also works","Avoid Chainsaw — Intangir is Deathproof so the death effect just misses (it already misses 25% of the time anyway) — and don't rely on Vanish+Doom, which no longer works in the Pixel Remaster","Land the killing blow accepting that whoever does eats one last Meteor — expect to lose them and still win the fight"],[],[33],[],"",null,null,null],["Esper Caves",1,"Defeating Ultros (3rd time)",["Enter with Terra, Locke, Strago (or preferred party) and grab the Healing Rod chest just inside (Healing Rod #1)","Work through Bonnacon/Adamankary inside — five bestiary entries here, and Bonnacons/Adamankaries are your Phase II grinding spot — and Land Grillon/Mandrake/Venobennu on the outside slopes","Against Venobennu pairs, hold off killing the second one so it uses Pearl Wind for Strago to learn","Reach the Warring Triad statue room and examine the statues","Fight off Ultros (his third encounter) guarding the path onward — don't use Water attacks on him, they heal him","Backtrack through the switch-triggered trapdoor rooms for the X-Potion, Chocobo Suit, and Tabby Suit chests","Reach the Esper chamber to end the segment; you're returned to Thamasa automatically"],["g14"],[18],[34],"wob",null,null,null],["Doma Castle — later",1,"",["GATED ON THE BANQUET — confirm you scored 50+ points at the Vector banquet (the Doma-withdrawal reward tier) before sailing back; the castle only reopens once the Empire withdraws, and falling short keeps Doma shut until the World of Ruin","Enter through the main gate; grab the Hi-Ether chest and examine the clock for an Elixir in the west rooms","Visit Cyan's family room (upper-right area) for the X-Potion chest","Follow the outer wall around to the last door for the Phoenix Down and Prayer Beads chests","If any of the first three items (Hi-Ether, Elixir, X-Potion) were missed here, they can still be picked up later in Cyan's Dream"],[],[],[35],"wob",null,null,null],["World of Balance — Act 1 Cleanup",1,"Triggering the Floating Continent",["This stop closes the moment you trigger the Floating Continent — treat everything below as due now, not optional","Sweep back through every earlier World of Balance stop for anything still outstanding; this list is duplicated from those story stops so you get one consolidated last pass instead of hunting piecemeal across the whole map, which only dilutes the pool for rarer Rages you still need on the Veldt","Prioritize any of the 9 combat-critical Rages not yet banked on the Veldt","Pick up any reachable missable bosses/chests/bestiary entries before triggering the Floating Continent","Missable enemies, bosses, and anything wanted for a Rage are also listed at their own story stop earlier in this list — tick either copy and both update"],[],[22,23,24,25,26,5,6,8,11,27,28,29,30,31,32],[],"wob",null,true,null],["END OF ACT I AUDIT",1,"Triggering the Floating Continent",["SPEND ALL REMAINING GIL FIRST — every shop in the world changes inventory or closes once Nelapa dies","Check overall bestiary/completion % via the Display Map in the MAIN MENU bestiary (not the in-field menu) — easy to miss","Cross-check your open-chest count against the target: 118 chests opened before the point of no return","Trigger the Floating Continent once satisfied everything is done"],["g15"],[],[],"once",null,null,null],["Esper Cave leveling",2,"",["Set the EXP boost to 4x in the Config/Boost menu","Take Gau alone to the Esper Cave's first screen and grind the Bonnacon/Adamankary encounters there","Equip Zona Seeker (Magic Power +2 per level-up) and cast Vanish on Gau before each fight — nothing in that fight can then touch him","Grind to level 26 — the last level everyone can reach before Sabin needs a Crusader level for 999 MP","Dual-stat Gau: skip Bahamut and Crusader entirely, backfill Bismarck afterward","While Gau is still 26, detour to Triangle Island for Intangir — that is the only realistic window","Leap Gau onto the Veldt afterward so his level stops counting toward party averages","Level recalculation points to keep in mind: Shadow recalculates at the Floating Continent, and every character re-recruited in the World of Ruin does too — but nothing recalculates when the three scenarios reunite, so low levels stay low through the rest of the World of Balance"],["g16"],[],[],"wob",null,null,null],["Air Force",3,"Defeating the main body",["Survive the Sky Armor/Spitfire skirmishes and the Ultros+Typhon fight on the way to the Floating Continent","Air Force immediately attacks afterward with its Laser Gun and Missile Bay parts still up — quicksave first as insurance","Focus fire on the Laser Gun ONLY, leaving Missile Bay alive, to make the Bit spawn (CONFIRMED for PR — two independent current sources agree, none support a kill-all-adds alternative)","Steal the X-Ether (#1) off the Laser Gun before it dies if you want it","Kill the Bit with physical attacks only — it absorbs any magic thrown at Air Force while alive","Clean up Missile Bay and the main body (weak to Lightning/Water)"],["g17"],[19],[],"once",null,null,null],["Floating Continent",3,"Approaching the Statues",["Land near the save point and use it","Explore the map, fighting Apokrypha/Behemoth/Brainpan/Misfit/Ninja/Platinum Dragon/Dragon and clearing the mandatory Gigantos fight (drops the Sasuke orb; Bio kills it in one turn) — eight bestiary entries total, four of them orb containers","DO NOT talk to Shadow yet — before finishing the whole map, jump back to the airship and Leap Gau onto the Veldt (strip his gear first, since his equipment goes with him and stays gone until you re-recruit him) so his level 26 doesn't inflate the party average and make Shadow join higher than needed","Return and talk to Shadow — he's stripped except his esper; recruit and re-equip him. He joins at the current, now-lower, party average (around level 6)","Grind Shadow plus one opposite-stat Break-caster (the Break-caster must boost the stat opposite Shadow's — e.g. Celes for Strength if Shadow's on Magic) to level 26: kill all but one enemy, KO everyone except those two, then finish the fight","Run from Ninja and Dragon during the grind — Break/Petrify doesn't land on either — but still clear one of each separately once for the bestiary","Once Shadow is done, level the rest of the active roster to 26 wherever you like, then proceed toward Ultima Weapon and the point of no return"],["g18"],[20],[36],"wob",null,null,["Level Shadow (joins at 6) plus one Strength Break-caster (Celes) to 26 here — everyone else can free-ride to 26 later, wherever you like"]],["Floating Continent — escape",3,"Jumping to the Blackjack",["Celes joins (if not already present); the six-minute escape timer starts","Fight through the Naude formations — they must be KILLED (Imp makes them flee and registers nothing for the bestiary); use Fire/Lightning/Holy-elemental attacks or Rasp on them (KO-based attacks miss)","Grab the Elixir orb by approaching from the south/east, not directly (the direct path collapses)","Defeat Nelapa (weak to Ice/Lightning/Holy, absorbs Fire) — offense only, the timer keeps running","Reach the jump point and wait there for Shadow instead of jumping immediately — jumping without him loses him AND everything he is carrying until the World of Ruin Coliseum","Jump to the Blackjack once Shadow appears (around the 0:04 mark)"],["g19"],[21],[],"once",null,null,null],["Solitary Island & Southern Continent",4,"",["LEVEL AVERAGING governs the whole World of Ruin: anyone you re-recruit is set to the average of your current members, rounded down — it never lowers a level, only raises it, so a straggler gets dragged up with no esper attached","Land in the World of Ruin; before leveling anyone, prioritize tracking down and recruiting the rest of the cast — find everyone first, then start leveling","Keep the EXP boost at 0x/off while the roster is still incomplete","Recruit each character, accepting that under-leveled ones get pulled up to the current party average (never down)","Once everyone is recruited, resume normal leveling/EXP boosts","At Solitary Island, fish and feed Cid only fast-moving fish — slow ones (and not feeding him at all) let his condition worsen and he dies"],[],[34,35],[],"",null,null,null],["Tzen — Collapsing House",4,"Helping the child",["Enter Tzen; an earthquake cutscene reveals Sabin holding up a collapsing house with a kid trapped inside.","Before entering, equip a Ribbon or Jeweled Ring on Celes — some enemies inside can Petrify, and a solo Petrify is a game over (buy a Jeweled Ring at the Relic Shop if needed).","Step to the door to start the 6-minute timer (it pauses on menu/map screens) and go in alone as Celes — this is TIMED, and everything inside (eight containers plus three entries) is lost for good once you help the kid, so grab it all now.","Clear the 8 chests: Healing Rod, Holy Rod, Ether, Hyper Wrist, two Monster-in-a-Box fights vs 4 Nightwalkers each, Blood Sword, Magicite Shard — multi-target Fira clears the Nightwalker/Zokka fights fast.","Reach the basement, talk to the kid, then get both of you back outside before time runs out.","The house collapses behind you; Sabin and Celes reunite and he joins the party for good.","Optional: buy the Seraph esper for 10 Gil from the man behind the Relic Shop if you skipped it in the World of Balance."],["g20"],[36],[37],"timed",[["Thief's Bracer",3000,"Locke — raises steal rate, needed for Kazekiri",null],["Alarm Earring",7000,"no back attacks",null],["Dragoon Boots",9000,"Mog",null],["Burning Fist",10000,"Sabin",null]],null,null],["Nikeah & Serpent Trench (WoR)",4,"",["From Tzen, cross the bridge east/north onto the Serpent Trench — it's above ground now and walkable on foot.","Fight through Trench encounters (Black Dragon, Delta Beetle, Vampire Thorn, Lizard, Devoahan — mostly Fire-weak); Sabin's Rising Phoenix clears groups quickly. Note: the Angler Whelk monster-in-a-box is not here — it's actually in Darill's Tomb, see that stop instead.","Mobliz sits partway along the Trench — detour there before continuing (see next stop).","Continue the Trench to its far end to reach Nikeah.","Shop Nikeah's refreshed gear (Rune Blade, Enhancer, elemental swords, new relics).","Visit the Pub, talk to the thieves, then tail their leader \"Gerad\" (Edgar in disguise) to the docks and stow away for South Figaro."],["g21"],[37],[],"",[["Gale Hairpin",8000,"more preemptive strikes — helps bestiary sweeps",null],["Hyper Wrist",8000,"Strength boost",null],["Prayer Beads",4000,"Evasion +20",null],["Zephyr Cloak",7000,"evasion",null],["Angel Ring",8000,"auto-Regen",null],["Rune Blade",7500,"Celes",null]],null,null],["Mobliz (WoR) — first visit",4,"",["Do this before sailing for Figaro — you're already on this continent, and Edgar isn't needed yet.","Enter Mobliz; sleep for free in the abandoned Relic Shop at the north of town, and grab the Phoenix Down from the barrel cluster near the ruined house west of the kid's house.","Follow the kid into the messenger's house (the old post office) and down to the basement.","Talk to the kids and to Terra — she refuses to fight.","Before leaving, equip Sabin with Venom Claws (dual + Genji Glove if you have them) and Quick Save — bring Sabin, since Celes alone makes the Humbaba fight genuinely dangerous.","Leave the house — Terra fights Humbaba alone and is scripted to lose (she's unequipped and can't hurt him); let her be KO'd, don't try to save her.","Celes and Sabin take over: use Poison/Bio damage, avoid any Thunder-based spells (Humbaba absorbs Lightning and heals from it).","Deal roughly 7500 damage and Humbaba flees; a kid runs up afterward and gives you the Fenrir magicite — a free esper this early is worth the trip alone.","Terra still refuses to join — leave town entirely; her recruitment arc resumes only after you have the Falcon."],[],[],[38],"",null,null,["MUST: Sabin — Celes alone makes Humbaba genuinely dangerous"]],["Figaro Continent & South Figaro (WoR)",4,"",["Take the thief ferry from Nikeah to South Figaro; this is your LAST CHANCE at the South Figaro outdoor containers (10 total, contents refreshed for WoR) — grab any barrels/boxes you skipped in the World of Balance.","Visit South Figaro Cave and refresh its 3 chests if you missed them earlier — also your last chance here.","Follow \"Gerad\" and the thieves through the cave to the hidden passage leading into Figaro Castle's basement.","Figaro Castle basement opens now — loot the B3F alcove chests (Crystal Helm, Gravity Rod, X-Potion, Hi-Ether) and the Royal Crown chest upstairs (five chests total).","Gear up (Reflect Rings + Hermes Sandals recommended) and fight the 4 Tentacles (bestiary #297-300) blocking the Engine Room — this is MANDATORY before Edgar rejoins, and he goes in completely unequipped, so gear everyone else well.","Edgar reveals himself and joins; search the throne-room statue for the hidden Soul Sabre.","Ride the castle to the surface (it resurfaces at Kohlingen) to continue."],[],[38,39],[39,40,41],"",[["Hermes Sandals",7000,"second copy",null],["Diamond Armor",15000,"front-liners",null],["Diamond Helm",8000,"front-liners — pairs with Diamond Armor",null],["Gold Lance",12000,"Mog",null]],null,null],["Kohlingen Continent",4,"",["Land on the Kohlingen continent and fight the local bestiary entries — four in the plains/forest (Bogy, Marchosias, Deepeye, Mousse), plus Sandhorse and Cancer if you head into the desert.","Shop Kohlingen: Dice (5000 Gil) is cheap and has a near-term use — damage = die x die x die x LEVEL x 2, ignoring defence and the Master's Scroll penalty entirely; Viper Darts (13000 Gil) is a strong but not-yet-needed weapon; and an Enhancer (10000 Gil) is worth grabbing to boost Celes's Magic stat.","Head to the Inn/Pub to find and recruit Setzer.","Note for later: the Fixed Dice sits only a few rooms into Kefka's Tower — a common tactic is an early raid just to grab it, then leave."],[],[40],[],"",[["Dice",5000,"Setzer",null],["Viper Darts",13000,"Setzer — better than Dice",null],["Enhancer",10000,"Celes — boosts Magic",null]],null,null],["Darill's Tomb",4,"",["Equip Ribbons/Amulets before entering — most enemies here are undead and several use Zombie/instant-death effects.","B1: optional Borghese fight (only found in this room).","B2: work the 6-door puzzle — grab the Crystal Mail and Regal Gown chests, then take the hidden path off the Regal Gown room (south-east corner, walk east into the wall) for the Growth Egg.","Examine all four southern gravestones (ERAU / QSSI / DLRO / WEHT) first — the lone north-west tombstone won't offer to carve until you have.","Take the north-west door and carve WEHT DLRO QSSI ERAU (\"THE WORLD IS SQUARE\" backwards) — sources disagree on the exact group order (WEHT/DLRO/QSSI/ERAU, or THEW/ORLD/ISSQ/UARE), so just arrange whatever groups it offers to spell the phrase — then grab the Genji Helm chest.","Use the turtles to cross to the save point; fight the Angler Whelk monster-in-a-box north-west of the save point for Dragon Claw(s) — try to kill the head and shell simultaneously, which is reported to drop 2 Dragon Claws instead of 1, though this isn't guaranteed (some sources say Pixel Remaster may always drop 2 regardless of kill method) — then grab the Man-Eater chest.","Heal up and remove any Reflect Rings — Dullahan punishes worn Reflect Rings with status ailments — then fight Dullahan guarding Darill's tomb: a mandatory fight that opens with a one-shot Lv.? Holy targeting anyone whose level divides evenly into your current Gil's last digit.","Follow Setzer down through the memory sequence to find the Falcon airship.","No shop here — it's a tomb; stock up in Maranda after you take the Falcon."],[],[41],[42],"",null,null,null],["Maranda (WoR)",4,"",["Land near Maranda now that you have the Falcon — Celes points you here straight after Darill's Tomb.","Talk to the ex-thief in the Inn and the woman between the shops for flavor hints.","Buy from the refreshed weapon/armor stock (Crystal Mail, Crystal Shield, Falchion, elemental scrolls, Tao Robe, Dark Gear) — the best armor on sale anywhere up to this point.","Talk to Lola, who has been reading letters from her boyfriend in Mobliz; read her latest letter and agree to write back, receiving the Lola's Letter key item.","Give the letter to the pigeon outside; watch it fly off toward Zozo, which is where the letters have been coming from.","Ahead in Zozo, buy the Rust-Rid (1000 Gil, from a man near the Inn) to open the roof door to Mt. Zozo and Cyan.","Optional: fight in the desert south of town for early Cactuar/Slagworm Gil and Magic AP."],[],[],[],"",[["Crystal Shield",7000,"Maranda WoR",null],["Magus Robe",13000,"best caster robe",null],["Crystal Mail",17000,"best heavy armour buyable",null]],null,null],["Mobliz (WoR) — return for Terra",4,"",["Requires the Falcon — you cannot trigger this on foot, so it waits until after Darill's Tomb; fly the Falcon back to Mobliz (this scene does not trigger by walking in).","Head to the messenger's house basement; learn that Katarin is missing.","Speak to the kids, then enter the house on the west side of town (Duane the wounded soldier's house); a dog follows you in and reveals a secret chamber behind the bookcase, where you find Katarin and Terra.","Grab the Hi-Ether from the pot before leaving.","Equip Thunder protection (Force Armor / Thunder Shield / Reflect Ring) and load up on Bio/Poison damage.","Leave the house — Humbaba attacks again with the same weaknesses (Poison) and absorption (Lightning), but this is actually two more back-to-back fights needing roughly triple the damage of the first Mobliz encounter, not just \"slightly stronger\" — he heals to full mid-scene when Terra joins.","Partway through he uses Humbaba Breath and blows two party members out of the fight; Terra then joins in Trance/Esper form (double attack and defense) as Humbaba heals back to full — finish him off for good this time.","Terra rejoins permanently; equip her with Relics and an Esper before moving on."],[],[],[46],"",null,null,null],["Mt. Zozo",4,"",["In Zozo town, buy Rust-Rid (1000 Gil) from the man near the Inn.","Use it on the rusted door atop the building marked \"Pub\" to open the path up to Mt. Zozo.","Consider casting Vanish/Phantom before entering — nearly every regular enemy here is a high-evasion physical attacker (a Sniper Eye also works).","Work through the cave picking up 5 chests: Ice Shield, Red Cap, Thunder Shield, Aegis Shield, Gold Hairpin — do NOT equip the Ice Shield for the boss fight (Storm Dragon's wind attacks double its wearer's damage).","Reach Cyan's hiding spot and read his confession letter to Lola; check his locked chest too — it gives Books the first time and is empty afterward, but both openings count toward the treasure total.","Cyan joins; if you want him in your active party, you'll need to backtrack to the Falcon and return.","Back at the save point, gear up (Thunder Shield is safe here, avoid the Ice Shield) and fight the Storm Dragon (weak to Lightning) — mandatory, guards the way back out, for a guaranteed Force Armor."],[],[42],[43],"",null,null,null],["Cave on the Veldt",4,"",["Enter the cave on the southwest side of the Veldt; follow Interceptor in.","Grab the Berserker Ring chest, then take the hidden-path detour to the north-west for the Death Warden monster-in-a-box, which drops a Tigerfang.","Grab the Ichigeki chest before flipping the section-3 switch — this is Shadow's ultimate weapon, don't sell it.","Stay invisible (Vanish/Phantom) all the way to the save point; equip Reflect Rings if you have them.","Fight the Living Behemoth King (an Imp spell trivializes it while you're invisible), then the Undead Behemoth King that ambushes immediately after — both mandatory.","You'll automatically fly the injured Shadow (or Relm, depending on your Floating Continent choice) to Thamasa afterward."],[],[43],[44],"",null,null,null],["Owzer's Mansion",4,"Defeating Chadarnook",["First pass, any time after recruiting Gau: try the stairs — a voice warns you off and Owzer's diary appears (the hint you're meant to get); examine the candelabra at the foot of the stairs to turn the lights on and proceed.","Examine the Flower painting in the north-east corner for a mandatory Rafflesia fight (Fire kills it fast) — this is missable and can't be triggered again once Chadarnook is defeated.","Examine the Gestahl portrait (west side) twice for the Emperor's Letter, which reveals the Phoenix Cave location.","Ignore the south-west woman painting for now — you'll come back to it on a second pass.","Second pass, after recruiting Shadow at the Coliseum: examine the south-west painting for the 2x Misty fight (rare steal: Moogle Suit).","Push through the chair-painting ambush, then grab the Moogle Suit chest and the hidden Lich Ring chest. Nearly every enemy in the mansion has an animal-suit rare steal, and those chain into Genji Armor at the Coliseum, so steal where you can.","Fight the encounters under all four floating chests (each triggers when you stand under its shadow): 293 Gil, Potion, Ether, and Gold Needle.","Examine the armor portrait for the Still Life fight — kill it with Fire to open the hidden boss door; rare steal is the Fake Mustache, which turns Sketch into Control.","Equip Lightning and Sleep protection, talk to Owzer, and defeat Chadarnook (target its Demon form, avoid attacking the Lakshmi form).","Get the Lakshmi magicite from the bookcase; Relm joins the party."],["g22"],[44],[45],"once",[["Jidoor's WoR shops",0,"The mansion is IN Jidoor — these are the town's shelves, not the dungeon's",null],["Circlet",7000,"Jidoor's shops, right outside the mansion — big Magic boost",null],["Black Cowl",7500,"Shadow / Locke",null],["Crystal Helm",10000,"Jidoor's shops, right outside the mansion — best helm on sale",null],["Black Garb",13000,"Shadow, Locke and Gogo",null]],null,null],["Phoenix Cave",4,"",["Land at the star-shaped mountain gap north of the southern continent near Tzen (its location comes from the Emperor's Letter found at Owzer's) and split into two parties of four — Party 1 fights the boss, so stack it.","Work the long but linear switch puzzle, swapping control each time a party reaches a dead end or a switch; grab the Teleport Stone, Wing Edge, Ribbon, and Dragon Horn chests — 5 of the 9 chests in the dungeon are empty but still count toward the total (the Phoenix chest can't be opened any other way).","Enemies here Zombify and some open with Death — bring Amulets or Ribbons, and the Lich Ring from Owzer's makes Death heal instead of kill.","The hook at the entrance takes you back to the Falcon if you want out mid-puzzle.","Regroup your strongest party, gear up in Fire resistance (or Rasp to strip its MP), and fight the Red Dragon (weak to Ice/Water) for a Murakumo.","Trigger the two remaining floor switches (one per party) to open the final path.","Follow the path to find Locke and the Phoenix Magicite — the scene auto-continues to Kohlingen.","In Kohlingen, watch the Rachel scene: Locke joins, you get the Phoenix esper, and he hands over everything that was in the \"empty\" chests (X-Potion, Phoenix Down, X-Ether, Elixir, Flame Shield, Valiant Knife)."],[],[45],[52],"",null,null,null],["Narshe (WoR) & Umaro's cave",4,"",["Arrive in Narshe, World of Ruin, with Locke in the party (required to unlock certain doors/scenes).","In the house up the stairs to the right of the Relic shop, talk to the sick old man to receive the Cursed Shield.","In the Mines, search the wall where Mog once stood for Molulu's Charm.","Open the three now-upgraded chests near the west mine entrance for a Ribbon, Guard Bracelet, and Elixir (no known lock-out — just don't forget them).","Equip the Cursed Shield on whoever will carry it — it inflicts every bad status while worn, so park it on someone durable and grind normally.","Win 256 battles (not 255 — the on-screen conversion message appears right after the 256th) to lift the curse and turn it into the Paladin's Shield. Solitary Island's wasteland, with a Ribbon equipped, is the recommended fast grinding spot.","Cultists' Tower fights, Coliseum fights, and any battle whose results screen gets skipped (Gau Leaping, everyone fleeing) do NOT count toward the 256 — don't expect to double-dip.","The Paladin's Shield teaches ULTIMA, your replacement for the Ragnarok magicite's Ultima.","Continue on to Umaro's cave (Yeti's Cave) as the next stop."],[],[48],[47,48],"",null,null,null],["Dinosaur Forest & WoR overworld",4,"",["Travel to the dinosaur-shaped forest north of the Veldt on the WoR overworld.","Fight random encounters for Tyrannosaur and Brachiosaur, both of which give large EXP.","Use these fights (with the right Magicite equipped) as an AP-farming spot for learning spells quickly — Brachiosaur is the best magicite AP farm in the game.","Optionally try to Steal a Ribbon from Brachiosaur."],[],[46,47],[],"",null,null,null],["Yeti's Cave",4,"",["Enter Yeti's Cave (near Narshe) with Mog in the party.","Fight through Tonberry encounters on the way in (they hit hard for this point in the run) — a chest here triggers a fight against 3 Tonberries with a small chance of a Minerva Bustier drop.","Push through to the Midgardsormr magicite.","Taking the magicite triggers a fight against Umaro, who is protective of it.","Defeat Umaro; with Mog present he joins the party afterward."],[],[49],[],"",null,null,null],["Triangle Island (WoR) — Zone Eater & Gogo's lair",4,"",["Travel to Triangle Island (the same island Intangir occupied in the WoB).","Fight the Zone Eater (optionally kill one first for its own bestiary entry), then let it Inhale your whole party — that's the only way in to Gogo.","Explore Zone Eater's Belly across three sub-floors (B1-B3), using the bridge-hopping and falling-ceiling puzzle rooms.","Collect all 9 chests down the bridges and under the falling roof (Hi-Ether, Red Jacket, Genji Armor, Magical Brush, Fake Mustache, Zephyr Cloak, Hero's Ring, Pinwheel, Thunder Shield).","Fight the six unique enemy formations inside for their bestiary entries (Covert, Kamui, Wartpuck, Shambling Corpse, Amduscias, Baalzephon).","Reach the door at the end and talk to Gogo to recruit him.","Leave via Teleport/Teleport Stone (or walk out) once done."],[],[50,52],[50],"",null,null,null],["Crescent Island (WoR)",4,"",["Travel to Crescent Island (Thamasa's island) in the World of Ruin.","Fight random encounters around the island to log its three exclusive bestiary entries: Vasegiatta, Gloomwind, Purusa.","Optionally bank Purusa's Rage (Land Slide, no elemental weakness) for Gau if he's in the party."],[],[51],[],"",null,null,null],["Cyan's Dream",4,"Defeating Wrexsoul",["Bring Cyan (mandatory) and at least one Steal-capable character — there's a missable Steal coming up — then enter Doma Castle in the WoR and save outside first.","Note before starting: this whole zone holds ELEVEN bestiary entries and vanishes for good the moment Wrexsoul dies, the largest single loss available in the World of Ruin — make sure everything below is done first.","Take a nap in the bedroom to trigger the Dreamscape.","Work through doors A-E of the Dreamscape to reassemble your party, fighting Alluring Rider, Weredragon, Coco, Pandora, and Parasite along the way (last chance for Alluring Rider/Weredragon).","Defeat the Dream Stooges boss trio (Curlax, Laragorn, Moebius) — you must actually kill Laragorn, not just have him flee, for his bestiary entry.","Continue through the dream Phantom Train and Magitek Armor cave sections, fighting Al Jabr, Io, Pluto Armor, and Schmidt (all last-chance encounters).","In the dream Doma Castle, grab any real-castle treasures still missing — they carry over — then proceed to the throne room.","Steal the Memento Ring (#3) from Wrexsoul during the boss fight, then defeat him outright — do not Banish/Snort/Odin him away or he won't log in the bestiary.","Collect the Masamune and the Alexander Esper before leaving — the whole dream zone and its exclusive bestiary entries vanish once Wrexsoul is dead."],["g24"],[53],[49],"once",null,null,null],["Ancient Castle",4,"",["Ride Figaro Castle underground (Edgar leading gives half-price shopping) and choose to stop exploring when the castle gets stuck.","Go to the jail; find the hidden doorway in the back of a cell leading into the connecting cave.","Work through the cave's three sections, collecting its 6 chests and beating the Master Tonberry monster-in-a-box.","Enter the Ancient Castle; defeat the Samurai Soul monster-in-a-box for the Master's Scroll — do NOT run from this fight, or you lose both the Scroll and the bestiary entry.","Examine the petrified Odin statue in the throne room for the Odin magicite, and grab the castle's remaining 4 chests plus the X-Ether item (eleven containers total across the cave's three sections and the castle).","Trigger the hidden staircase near the queen's throne to reach and defeat the Blue Dragon.","Examine the petrified queen to upgrade Odin into Raiden (irreversible), then walk back to Figaro Castle — there's no Teleport out."],["g23"],[54],[51],"",null,null,null],["Cultists' Tower",4,"",["Assemble a strong all-magic party (ideally your four best mages, e.g. Terra/Celes/Relm/Strago; Umaro can also fight normally here, or use Gogo mimicking Magic if short a caster).","MAGIC ONLY inside: no Attack, Steal, Sketch, Lore, or Rage anywhere in the tower — the only permitted commands besides Magic are Items (needed for healing), Summon, Mimic, and Umaro's berserk attacks. Bring casters and plenty of MP.","Equip for Magic/Magic Defense/Magic Evasion (physical stats don't matter) and cast Float before entering — Quake shows up often.","Climb the tower's four ascents (it has no numbered floors), grabbing one hidden-room chest per storeroom floor: Safety Bit, Air Anchor (via a secret room found by examining a wall on the first ascent), Genji Shield, Kagenui, and Force Armor.","Defeat the Holy Dragon monster-in-a-box partway up (Silence shuts it down completely) for the Holy Lance.","At the top, take the Soul of Thamasa from the chest in the penthouse before the final fight.","Defeat Magic Master (Reraise + Reflect Ring stalling, or draining its MP, are the standard plans) for a Megalixir.","Fight your way back down and out — no Teleport inside the tower."],[],[55],[53],"",null,null,null],["Ebot's Rock",4,"",["Reach Ebot's Rock and step on the floor switches, which teleport you semi-randomly around the cave.","Open chests along the way — each holds 1-5 pieces of Coral, and chests refill every time you're teleported, so Coral can be farmed indefinitely.","Find the hungry statue/chest and feed it 22 Coral all at once (partial feeds are simply consumed without progress) to unlock the way forward.","Push on to Hidon; defeat its Erebus escorts first so Hidon uses Grand Delta, the only way to learn that Lore."],[],[56],[58],"",null,null,null],["Coliseum",4,"",["Reach the Coliseum north of Kohlingen — it only opens for betting in the WoR (in the WoB you can still grab the Hero's Ring from a pot outside).","Save before every bet: Coliseum fights are strictly auto-battle (no manual control), so even 'safe' bets can be lost to bad luck.","Use the Coliseum Bet Table to plan chains toward specific rewards (e.g., bet Ragnarok against Daedalus for the Lightbringer).","Fight Siegfried if going for his (tough) optional bestiary entry.","Treat Coliseum wins as bestiary-only — wagered wins do NOT register the formation for Gau's Veldt/Rage-learning purposes."],[],[57],[],"",null,null,null],["Ragnarok",4,"Choice made",["With Locke in the party, visit the weapon shop in Narshe, World of Ruin, and talk to the shopkeeper.","Choose SWORD (melt the magicite into the Ragnarok sword) or MAGICITE (keep it as an Esper that teaches Ultima) — never both.","If you took the sword: bet it against Daedalus at the Coliseum to win the Lightbringer, the best sword in the game — this is the only way to get it, but it also gives up the Ragnarok magicite's Metamorphose summon.","If you took the magicite: equip it to teach Ultima directly, but you give up the Lightbringer.","Either way, recover the missing Ultima source later via the Cursed Shield -> Paladin's Shield grind, which also teaches Ultima.","Do not plan around stealing extra Ragnaroks from Lady in the final battle — PR closed that loophole; items stolen there are discarded once you save after the ending, so only one sword/Lightbringer is obtainable."],["g25"],[],[],"once",null,null,null],["Kefka's Tower",4,"Final battle",["Stock up on Megalixirs/X-Potions before entering — there are no shops inside.","Split your 12 strongest characters into three balanced parties (put Strago in Party 1 for a later exclusive Lore, and keep Steal-capable characters like Locke and Gogo in different parties).","Work each party's path, switching between them at the marked points, collecting the tower's 16 chests along the way, plus one hidden Ribbon.","Steal the Force Armor (#4) from the Guardian boss — it's limited in quantity and won't be offered again.","Have Strago learn Force Field from the Fiend boss — she's the only enemy in the game who uses it.","Clear the remaining Legendary Dragon and 'statue' bosses (Guardian, Demon, Fiend, Goddess) to reunite the parties.","Proceed to the final battle against Kefka."],["g26"],[58],[54,55,56,57],"",null,null,null]];
